The bug was caused by the use of hard-coded strings ("AMBARI_SERVER" and "AMBARI") in multiple locations throughout the codebase, which made the code less maintainable and prone to errors if the component names were changed or referenced inconsistently. This could lead to issues in functionality where the system fails to recognize or properly handle the Ambari server component.

